meta {
  name: Get Patient Dues
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/patient-dues?patientId={{patientId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  patientId: {{patientId}}
  ~excludeOrderId: {{orderId}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Returns the patient's outstanding **previous dues** for the Create Order screen
  (/registration/create), resolved both at the active branch and business-wide:

  ```
  {
    "outstanding": number,              // CURRENT branch only — the "Clear
                                        //   Previous Dues" cap + the previous-dues
                                        //   gate (dues are collected/cleared per
                                        //   branch, so these ignore other branches)
    "businessWideOutstanding": number,  // all branches (collapses to `outstanding`
                                        //   without the cross-branch permission)
    "branches": [                       // per-branch breakdown (active branch first;
      {                                 //   only the active branch without permission)
        "branchId": string,
        "branchName": string,
        "isActive": boolean,            // false ⇒ "Inactive here." (never collectable)
        "isCurrentBranch": boolean,     // true ⇒ Collect Here = Yes
        "orderCount": number,           // orders carrying a due at this branch
        "totalDue": number,
        "oldestDueOrderDate": string | null
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Each figure is the summed positive `netAmount − paidAmount` across the patient's
  active, non-cancelled orders (`ORDER`/`APPOINTMENT`).

  Optional `excludeOrderId` — pass the order currently being EDITED so its OWN
  unpaid balance is excluded from the total. Without it, editing an order with a
  balance would show that balance as the patient's "previous dues" and prompt the
  operator to clear it — yet the finalize-time previous-dues gate EXCLUDES the
  order being finalized, so it would then reject the clearance as an overpayment
  of ₹0. Passing `excludeOrderId` makes the screen's figure and the gate agree.

  Cross-branch visibility is
  gated by `View cross-branch results`
  (`registration:create_order_patient_details__view_cross_branch_results`); without
  it, `businessWideOutstanding` equals `outstanding` and `branches` contains only
  the active branch — other branches' dues are never leaked. Branch + cross-branch
  permission come from the JWT. 422 `ORDER_PATIENT_NOT_FOUND` if the patient is not
  in the tenant.
}
